# FIXED, DEFECT 2208, 2026-10-25, M-rechecked-issues.
#
# SYMPTOM: two modules that each bind `K_DIV`, a value C leaves undefined,
# were told `ffi_constant_type` twice, both at the first module's binding,
# and never at the second's, with no refusal anywhere.
#
# CAUSE: the value check placed a finding by its constant's NAME
# (`ffi_lookup.declaration`, the first group declaring it), where the
# accessor it read holds its own declaration (`cli/value_told.hero`).
#
# FIX: the finding is placed at the accessor's own declaration
# (`ffi_lookup.declared_at`), so each module is told at its own line.
use fixedbugs2208/div_a
use fixedbugs2208/div_b

function main()
    print(div_a.a() + div_b.b())
